"Internal Error ()\nciteturn631view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://press.stripe.com/maintenance\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: URL https://press.stripe.com/maintenance is not accessible via this tool.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAbout – sirjamesjeans (https://sirjamesjeans.com/about/)\nciteturn631view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://sirjamesjeans.com/about/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 75\nL0: 【0†sirjamesjeans】\nL1: \nL2: [Input] Menu expanded collapsed\nL3: \nL4:   * 【0†Home】\nL5:   * 【1†About】\nL6:   * 【2†Buy】\nL7: # About\nL8: \nL9: Sir James Jeans, Scientist, Philosopher and Musician. Through Space and Time in the first half of the 20th Century\nL10: \nL11: Authors: Alexander Kozenko & Christopher Jeans\nL12: \nL13: 296 pages with 200+ illustrations.\nL14: \nL15: Dimensions: 26×18.5cm\nL16: \nL17: Paperback\nL18: \nL19: ISBN: 978-1-5272-7855-4\nL20: \nL21: RRP: £25\nL22: Sir James Jeans (1877-1946) has been described as “a mathematician, astronomer, physicist, musician, a brilliant writer and lecturer, one who could truly be described as a Renaissance man”.  He was “a giant in an age of gigantic developments in science and he had a great and honourable share in the making of that age”.\nL23: \nL24: Who was this man and what were his achievements?\nL25: This biography describes Jeans’s contribution to science, astrophysics in particular and takes you behind behind the scenes of a very private and shy man. It describes the major role his two wives Charlotte Mitchell (1877-1934) and the musician Susi Hock (1911-1993) played in his success. It brings together three families: The Jeanses with their newspaper background, the Tiffanys of New York jewellery fame, and the Hocks, a notable Viennese family.\nL26: It describes Jeans’s background, his private and professional lives, and details the development of Cleveland Lodge, his home, as an international musical centre. The book is profusely illustrated using contemporary photographs from the family albums and other sources. It includes the most comprehensive bibliography of his writings, published and unpublished, that is available.\nL27: Table of Contents\nL28: \nL29: Introduction\nL30: \nL31: Growing Up in the 19th Century\nL32: \nL33: Newspapers and the Jeans Clan\nL34: \nL35: Cambridge 1896-1905\nL36: \nL37: Princeton and Marriage to Charlotte Mitchell 1905-1909\nL38: \nL39: Cambridge and Dorking 1909-1919\nL40: \nL41: The Royal Society and The Royal Astronomical Society 1919-1929\nL42: \nL43: Stellar Dynamics\nL44: \nL45: The Twilight Years, Popular Writing and Public Outreach\nL46: \nL47: A Musical Marriage, Susi Hock\nL48: \nL49: Boxhill Music Festival\nL50: \nL51: Physics and Philosophy\nL52: \nL53: The Final Years\nL54: \nL55: Cleveland Lodge, its Fate\nL56: \nL57: Kozenko’s Scholarly Biography\nL58: BIBLIOGRAPHY\nL59: \nL60: Like\nL61: \nL62: 【0†sirjamesjeans】,\nL63: \nL64:   * 【3†Privacy】\nL65:   *     * 【0†sirjamesjeans】\nL66:     * 【4†Sign up†wordpress.com】\nL67:     * 【5†Log in†wordpress.com】\nL68:     * 【6†Copy shortlink†wp.me】\nL69:     * 【7†Report this content†wordpress.com】\nL70:     * 【8†Manage subscriptions†subscribe.wordpress.com】\nL71: \nL72: 【9†iframe†widgets.wp.com】\nL73: \nL74: 【10†Image†pixel.wp.com】\n"
